    {
      "source": "Doctors of Running",
      "priority": 3,
      "url": "https://www.doctorsofrunning.com/2024/11/asics-novablast-5-review-2024.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: FF Blast Max gives a softer, high-stack ride than v4 with strong impact protection; heel transitions feel smooth, while the forefoot is slightly stiff but distinctly bouncier.",
        "Responsiveness: Energy return is moderate with clear bounce (especially in the forefoot), good for strides and pace pickups, but it is not a highly snappy or truly propulsive ride.",
        "Stability: A more structured upper improves forefoot security, and the moderately stiff heel counter/rigid rearfoot plus slightly stiff midfoot improve lateral control versus v4.",
        "Durability: Outsole wear appears excellent (reviewers noted little to no wear after ~40 miles), and midsole cushioning retained resilience/compliance, indicating above-average material longevity."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Road Trail Run",
      "priority": 4,
      "url": "https://www.roadtrailrun.com/2024/11/asics-novablast-5-iniital-review-fun.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The 41.5/33.5 mm stack with FF Blast Max gives high impact protection and a plush, softer ride than v4, though one tester noted it can feel a bit stiff at slower paces.",
        "Responsiveness: FF Blast Max is described as quicker-reacting than FF Blast Plus, with strong energy return and a noticeably snappier, more agile toe-off versus Novablast 4.",
        "Stability: Support is limited for pronation/slow heel-strike running due to soft foam, a narrower platform, minimal midfoot structure, and a short rigid heel counter despite slightly improved heel hold.",
        "Durability: Long-term wear is not yet reported; early notes mention the new outsole can trap small pebbles, while the upper includes a substantial toe bumper for added front-end protection."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Believe in the Run",
      "priority": 5,
      "url": "https://believeintherun.com/shoe-reviews/asics-novablast-5-review/",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: FF Blast Max gives a very soft, premium max-cushion ride with strong impact protection and notably generous forefoot cushioning, making it highly comfortable for daily and long runs.",
        "Responsiveness: The softer setup is less snappy for faster efforts (it can feel like you are working against it), though the forefoot pod adds a mild trampoline-like toe-off.",
        "Stability: For a high-stack, soft shoe, it is reported as surprisingly stable and not precarious, indicating dependable platform/lateral control.",
        "Durability: The shoe keeps the AHAR LO outsole (with slightly changed pattern/coverage); traction is noted as mediocre, and clear long-term wear/longevity results are not established in the provided text."
      ]
    }
